# Both Dockerfiles start with `COPY . .` in the pruner stage, so without this
# file the whole working tree goes into an image layer. That was 350MB of
# context per build, and it included two things that must never be in an
# image at all: the .env file and the documents directory, which on a real
# deployment holds patient records.

# Secrets.
.env
.env.*

# Patient documents and database dumps. Both are volumes at runtime.
storage
**/storage
backups

# Rebuilt inside the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
.turbo
**/.turbo

# Not part of a build.
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
docs
e2e
playwright.config.ts
playwright-report
test-results
coverage
**/coverage
*.log
npm-debug.log*
Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
README.md
